From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:48:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: Add the Apple VFL and SwissPPNFTL translation layer

iOS stores its disk on PPN NAND through Apple's VFL and SwissPPNFTL. Recover
the 64 GB layout from the replicated VFL contexts and lane tables, decode
the saved SFTL ranges and replay the journal written after them, including
completed-block summaries and open stripes with holes. Unsupported formats
and incomplete sequences fail before a disk is registered.

Expose the 64,000,000,000-byte logical medium as the applesftlN block
device. Requests use a preallocated buffer, and a failed storage read stops
further I/O.

The format rules are ported from Orchard's P105 Python reference. KUnit
tests build complete synthetic media for checkpoint recovery, journal and
trim ordering, replica disagreement, torn summaries and runtime failure;
they contain no captured device data.

[Orchard: from shaynelegault/orchard#89 ffa74e8 (source e7d118292);
 dropped the read budget and lifetime module parameters of the following
 source patch; shortened the commit message]

